    "Repair round 1/3 (fix 2): Replaced `past(...)` (not available in this Chisel LTL version) with explicit `RegNext` sampling. `turn_flip_on_exit` now uses `val was_in_l6 = RegNext(pc(self)===L6, false.B)` to snapshot the L6 condition from the previous cycle, since `turn:=~self` in L6 takes effect at the next clock edge. Liveness assertions unchanged (already `delayRange(1,1)`). All assertion labels preserved exactly.",
    "Repair round 2/3: Fixed `turn_flip_on_exit` assertion by adding `val self_prev = RegNext(self)` and comparing `turn === ~self_prev` instead of `turn === ~self`. Root cause: when `io_select` changes simultaneously with process 1 exiting L6, `self` updates to the new value at the same cycle that `turn := ~self` (computed from old self) takes effect. The assertion incorrectly compared `turn` (computed from old self=1, resulting in 0) against `~new_self` (for new self=0, ~0=1). Fix samples the old self value with RegNext, matching the register assignment timing. The assertion label `turn_flip_on_exit` is preserved exactly. No homologous assertions exist — this is the only assertion comparing `turn` against `~self`."
